T-009 blast-radius regression (revised, both runtimes):
plugins/sdd-quality-loop/scripts/emit-run-record.{sh,ps1} is a cross-epic
shared surface (Security Boundary B2, third named B2 file).

Correction over the prior coder-regression.log (this same directory): that log's
enumeration technique was 'grep -l emit-run-record tests/*.tests.sh' -- a .sh-only
glob that structurally cannot match a PowerShell suite, so no .ps1 consumer of the
modified emit-run-record.ps1 was ever enumerated or run. Re-inspection also found
that the ORIGINAL .sh-side enumeration itself over-matched: two of its five listed
suites (tests/check-component-coverage.tests.sh, tests/validate-capability-registry.tests.sh)
never actually invoke emit-run-record.sh -- the grep hit is a comment mention
('# TEST-054 ... emit-run-record', check-component-coverage.tests.sh:217) and a
synthetic fixture filename used to prove a scanner ignores non-check-* scripts
('emit-run-record.py', validate-capability-registry.tests.sh:82), never a real
invocation of the script. Both still ran clean in the original log, so this did
not hide a regression, but it did overstate the true blast-radius consumer count.

Revised technique: grep -lE 'emit-run-record\.(sh|ps1)' across both tests/*.tests.sh
AND tests/*.tests.ps1, then each match manually inspected to confirm it is a genuine
invocation (a call to the real script path), never a comment or fixture-string
mention.

Genuine .sh invokers (3): tests/emit-run-record-feature-scope.tests.sh (T-009's own
suite), tests/effort-policy-flip.tests.sh (TEST-044 shells out to emit-run-record.sh,
but is SKIPped unless SDD_ALLOW_REAL_CODEX_SMOKE=1 is set -- so the script is not
actually exercised by this run; disclosed, not excluded), tests/run-panelist-effort.tests.sh
(EMIT_RUN_RECORD_SH, invoked at its own line 326).

Genuine .ps1 invokers (2): tests/emit-run-record-feature-scope.tests.ps1 (T-009's own
suite), tests/run-panelist-effort.tests.ps1 ($emitRunRecordPs1, invoked at its own
line 330). tests/effort-policy-flip.tests.ps1 is NOT a genuine .ps1 consumer despite
matching the earlier grep -l pass on 'emit-run-record.ps1' in a comment: its own
TEST-044 is written to always Skip and defer to the .sh twin even when opted in
('single real-invocation path, avoids double LLM spend across both lanes',
effort-policy-flip.tests.ps1:127-132) -- it never calls emit-run-record.ps1. Included
below anyway for full parity/transparency with the .sh side's inclusion.

run-all.sh/.ps1 is still not used here for the same reason as the prior log: this
repository's own deterministic-lane self-check fails closed until a human applies
the staged human-copy CI patch (precedent: T-004's own qg-cycle2/T-004/regression.log).

